# Pishe frontend rules

- Atoms: presentational only — no `features`, `store`, or `next/navigation`
- Molecules: presentational; no `organisms` or `features` (ThemeToggle may use UI store)
- Organisms / features: may use Query, store, and domain UI
- Server data via TanStack Query in `features/*/queries.ts`
- Client never imports Prisma; only `/api/v1/*`
- UI copy via next-intl (`resources/messages/fa`), not hardcoded Persian in JSX
- Follow `apps/pishe/docs/product-copy.md` — never expose Keycloak, logs, operators, realms, or infra to end users
- Spacing: semantic tokens (`gap-mol`, `p-pad-mol-md`, `h-control`) — avoid raw `p-4` / `gap-6` in new code
